# s2b-tunnel core wiring

## 1. Dependency edge (mixdog-ssh -> mixdog-workspace)
tunnel.rs picks the local port with `mixdog_workspace::pageserver::ports::bind_loopback` (the one fetch-safe loopback port rule of the
tree; the tunnel's tests also read `FETCH_BLOCKED_PORTS`). No cycle: mixdog-workspace does not depend on mixdog-ssh.

In crates/mixdog-ssh/Cargo.toml [dependencies], after the `mixdog-app-server-client` line:

    mixdog-workspace = { workspace = true }

and in Cargo.lock add `"mixdog-workspace",` to the dependency list of the `mixdog-ssh` package (alphabetical place, after `"mixdog-statefile"` /
`"mixdog-spawn"` entries as the sort puts it), because the build is --locked.

## 2. Modules
lib.rs of mixdog-ssh already lists `pub mod tunnel;` and `pub mod callback_forward;`; nothing to add. `tunnel` declares its own test module
(`tunnel_tests.rs`, which also holds the callback forward's tests).

## 3. SERVICE_PENDING
No protocol method is served by these two modules; nothing to remove. A task that connects a remote host starts them:
`SshTunnel::start(env, ctx, TunnelSpec)` and `open_callback_forward(env, ctx, target, port)`.
